    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0642" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10678: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-13T16:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>…There is no intimation as yet of reopening navigation on West River. British
                    gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Sea Mew</hi> is now en route to Wuchow with food
                    supplies for foreigners, including Americans if needed.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
